+# tasks-api
+
+A multi-tenant task-tracking HTTP API built with [Bun](https://bun.sh),
+[Elysia](https://elysiajs.com), and [Drizzle ORM](https://orm.drizzle.team) on SQLite
+(via libSQL). Organizations own users, projects, and tasks. Clients authenticate with
+bearer tokens.
+
+## Running locally
+
+Requirements: Bun 1.4.3 (pinned in `package.json` under `packageManager`).
+
+```sh
+# 1. Install dependencies
+bun install
+
+# 2. Configure the environment (Bun loads .env automatically)
+cp .env.example .env
+
+# 3. Create the directory for the SQLite file. The migrator does not create it
+#    and fails if it is missing.
+mkdir -p data
+
+# 4. Apply migrations from ./drizzle
+bun run db:migrate
+
+# 5. Load demo data (see "Seed data" below)
+bun run db:seed
+
+# 6. Start the dev server with file watching
+bun run dev
+```
+
+The server listens on `http://localhost:4000` by default. Check it with:
+
+```sh
+curl http://localhost:4000/api/health
+# {"status":"ok"}
+```
+
+The server also applies pending migrations at startup, so step 4 is only required
+before seeding.
+
+### Seed data
+
+`db:seed` inserts fixed IDs and does **not** clear existing data. If you run it a second
+time against the same database, it fails with a unique-constraint error. To reset,
+delete the database file and run the migration and seed again:
+
+```sh
+rm -f data/dev.db && bun run db:migrate && bun run db:seed
+```
+
+The seed creates two organizations. All users have the password `password123`.
+
+| Organization          | User                            | Role   | Bearer token             |
+| --------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------ | ------------------------ |
+| Acme (`org_acme`)     | `ada@acme.test` (`usr_ada`)     | admin  | `dev-acme-admin-token`   |
+| Acme (`org_acme`)     | `bob@acme.test` (`usr_bob`)     | member | `dev-acme-member-token`  |
+| Globex (`org_globex`) | `gina@globex.test` (`usr_gina`) | admin  | `dev-globex-admin-token` |
+
+The seeded tokens are valid for ten years. They are for local development and tests
+only.
+
+Seeded projects: `prj_web`, `prj_app`, `prj_billing` (Acme), `prj_infra` (Globex).
+Seeded tasks: `tsk_1` to `tsk_5` (Acme), `tsk_6` (Globex).
+
+### Other scripts
+
+| Script                 | Purpose                                          |
+| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
+| `bun run start`        | Start the server without file watching           |
+| `bun run build`        | Bundle to `dist/`                                |
+| `bun run test`         | Run the Vitest suite (`src/**/*.test.ts`)        |
+| `bun run typecheck`    | `tsc --noEmit`                                   |
+| `bun run lint`         | ESLint                                           |
+| `bun run format:check` | Prettier check (`format:fix` to write)           |
+| `bun run db:generate`  | Generate a new migration from `src/db/schema.ts` |
+
+The test setup (`src/test/setup.ts`) supplies its own defaults for `LOG_LEVEL`,
+`WEBHOOK_SECRET`, and `TOKEN_TTL_HOURS`, so tests need no `.env`.
+
+## Environment variables
+
+| Variable          | Default            | Used by                            | Description                                                                                                    |
+| ----------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `PORT`            | `4000`             | server                             | HTTP port.                                                                                                     |
+| `DATABASE_URL`    | `file:data/dev.db` | server, migrate, seed, drizzle-kit | libSQL connection URL.                                                                                         |
+| `WEBHOOK_SECRET`  | _none_             | `POST /api/webhooks/billing`       | Shared secret expected in the `x-webhook-secret` header. If unset, every webhook request is rejected with 401. |
+| `TOKEN_TTL_HOURS` | `24`               | `POST /api/auth/token`             | Lifetime of tokens issued by the login endpoint.                                                               |
+| `LOG_LEVEL`       | `info`             | logger                             | One of `debug`, `info`, `warn`, `error`, `silent`. Logs are JSON lines on stdout (warn/error on stderr).       |
+
+## Authentication
+
+Endpoints marked **auth** require `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Get a token from
+`POST /api/auth/token`, or use one of the seeded tokens.
+
+- If the header is missing or malformed, the response is `401 {"code":"unauthenticated","message":"missing bearer token"}`.
+- If the token is unknown or expired, the response is `401 Unauthorized` (plain text).
+
+Data is scoped to the caller's organization, with the exception noted for
+`GET /api/tasks/:id`.
+
+## Endpoints
+
+When a request body fails schema validation, the API returns Elysia's default validation
+error (status 422, JSON with `type: "validation"`). Unknown routes return
+`404 Not Found`.
+
+### Health
+
+#### `GET /api/health`
+
+Returns `200 {"status":"ok"}`. No auth.
+
+### Auth
+
+#### `POST /api/auth/token`
+
+Exchanges email and password for a new bearer token. No auth.
+
+```json
+{ "email": "ada@acme.test", "password": "password123" }
+```
+
+- `200 {"token": "...", "expiresAt": "<ISO timestamp>"}`
+- `401 {"error":"invalid email or password"}`
+
+#### `GET /api/me` (auth)
+
+Returns the current user: `{ id, orgId, role, email, name }`.
+
+### Projects
+
+#### `GET /api/projects` (auth)
+
+Lists the organization's projects ordered by name, each with task counts per status:
+
+```json
+{
+  "items": [
+    {
+      "id": "prj_web",
+      "name": "Website relaunch",
+      "description": "New marketing site",
+      "createdAt": "2026-10-01T09:00:00.000Z",
+      "taskCounts": { "todo": 1, "in_progress": 1, "done": 1 }
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+#### `POST /api/projects` (auth)
+
+| Field         | Type   | Rules                  |
+| ------------- | ------ | ---------------------- |
+| `name`        | string | required, 1–100 chars  |
+| `description` | string | optional, ≤ 2000 chars |
+
+Returns `201` with the created project row.
+
+#### `GET /api/projects/:id` (auth)
+
+Returns the project, or `404 Project not found` (plain text).
+
+#### `GET /api/projects/:id/tasks` (auth)
+
+Returns `{"items": [Task, ...]}` ordered by creation time, or `404 Project not found`.
+
+#### `POST /api/projects/:id/tasks` (auth)
+
+| Field         | Type    | Rules                                |
+| ------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------ |
+| `title`       | string  | required, 1–200 chars                |
+| `description` | string  | optional, ≤ 5000 chars               |
+| `isUrgent`    | boolean | optional, default `false`            |
+| `assigneeId`  | string  | optional, must be a user in your org |
+| `dueDate`     | string  | optional, `YYYY-MM-DD`               |
+
+- `201` with the created Task.
+- `400 {"error":"assignee must be a member of your organization"}`.
+- `404 Project not found`.
+
+When the task has an assignee, the API emails them an assignment notification. Locally,
+the mailer writes a `mail.sent` log line and sends nothing.
+
+### Tasks
+
+The Task object looks like this:
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "tsk_3",
+  "projectId": "prj_web",
+  "title": "Fix broken signup link",
+  "description": null,
+  "status": "todo",
+  "isUrgent": true,
+  "assigneeId": "usr_ada",
+  "dueDate": null,
+  "createdAt": "2026-10-01T09:03:00.000Z",
+  "updatedAt": "2026-10-01T09:03:00.000Z"
+}
+```
+
+`status` is one of `todo`, `in_progress`, `done`.
+
+#### `GET /api/tasks/:id` (auth)
+
+Returns the Task, or `404 {"error":"task not found"}`.
+
+> **Note:** Unlike the other endpoints, this one does not check the task's organization.
+> Any authenticated user can read any task by ID.
+
+#### `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` (auth)
+
+Partial update. Every field is optional:
+
+| Field         | Type                              | Notes                                        |
+| ------------- | --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
+| `title`       | string (≤ 200)                    | Trimmed; cannot be blank                     |
+| `description` | string (≤ 5000) \| null           |                                              |
+| `status`      | `todo` \| `in_progress` \| `done` | See transition rules below                   |
+| `isUrgent`    | boolean                           |                                              |
+| `assigneeId`  | string \| null                    | Must be a user in your org; `null` unassigns |
+| `dueDate`     | `YYYY-MM-DD` \| null              |                                              |
+
+Status transitions:
+
+- `todo` → `in_progress`
+- `in_progress` → `todo` or `done`
+- `done` → `todo` (admins only)
+
+Errors:
+
+| Status | Body `error`                                     |
+| ------ | ------------------------------------------------ |
+| 400    | `title cannot be blank`                          |
+| 400    | `assignee must be a member of your organization` |
+| 403    | `only admins can reopen finished tasks`          |
+| 404    | `task not found`                                 |
+| 409    | `cannot move a task from <from> to <to>`         |
+| 409    | `assign the task before marking it done`         |
+| 409    | `finished tasks cannot get a new due date`       |
+
+If the request changes nothing, the API returns the task unchanged. When the update
+assigns someone new, the API sends them the assignment notification.
+
+#### `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` (auth, admin only)
+
+- `204` on success.
+- `403 Forbidden` (plain text) for non-admins.
+- `404 {"error":"task not found"}`.
+
+### Webhooks
+
+#### `POST /api/webhooks/billing`
+
+Billing-provider webhook. It does not use bearer auth. Instead, it requires the header
+`x-webhook-secret: <WEBHOOK_SECRET>`.
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "evt_123",
+  "type": "payment.succeeded",
+  "data": { "orgId": "org_acme", "credits": 50 }
+}
+```
+
+- For `payment.succeeded`, the API adds `data.credits` (a non-negative integer,
+  default 0) to the organization's credit balance. Other event types are accepted and
+  ignored.
+- `200 {"received":true}`.
+- `401 invalid webhook secret` (plain text).
+
+Credits are added each time an event is received; duplicate deliveries of the same `id`
+are not detected.
